"pos": "n.",
"meaning": "蔬菜；植物人；呆板懒散的人；植物；植物的",
"translations": [
"n. 蔬菜；植物人；呆板懒散的人；植物",
"adj. 植物的"
],
"en_defs": [
"Any plant.",
"A plant raised for some edible part of it, such as the leaves, roots, fruit or flowers, but excluding any plant considered to be a fruit, grain, herb, or spice in the culinary sense.",
"The edible part of such a plant.",
"A person whose brain (or, infrequently, body) has been damaged so that they cannot interact with the surrounding environment; a person in a persistent vegetative state.",
"Of or relating to plants.",
"Of or relating to vegetables."
],
"examples": [
{
"en": "A good general diet should include plenty of fresh vegetables.",
"cn": "一份良好的日常饮食应当包括大量的新鲜蔬菜。"
},
{
"en": "...compounds of animal, vegetable or mineral origin.",
"cn": "…来自动物、植物或矿物的化合物。"
},
{
"en": "The <b>vegetable</b> harvest is disastrously behind schedule.",
"cn": "蔬菜收割灾难性地滞后于计划。"
},
{
"en": "Peas, beans and lentils are a good source of <b>vegetable</b> protein.",
"cn": "豌豆、豆荚和扁豆是植物蛋白质的大好来源。"
},
{
"en": "As a general rule <b>vegetable</b> oils are better for you than animal fats.",
"cn": "一般来说，植物油比动物脂肪对人较有好处。"
}
],
