"pos": "n.",
"meaning": "投资；值得买的东西；（时间、精力的）投入；<旧>包围，封锁",
"translations": [
"n. 投资；值得买的东西；（时间、精力的）投入；<旧>包围，封锁"
],
"en_defs": [],
"examples": [
{
"en": "He said the government must introduce tax incentives to encourage investment.",
"cn": "他说，政府必须通过给予税收利益来鼓励投资。"
},
{
"en": "...an investment of twenty-eight million dollars.",
"cn": "…2800万美元的投资额。"
},
{
"en": "When selecting boots, fine, quality leather will be a wise investment.",
"cn": "在挑选靴子时，买精致、质量上乘的皮靴会是明智的。"
},
{
"en": "I worry about this big investment of time not working.",
"cn": "我担心这么多的时间投入不起作用。"
},
{
"en": "Training is an <b>investment</b> not a cost.",
"cn": "培训是一种投资而不是一种花费。"
},
{
"en": "<b>Investment</b> is all about running risks.",
"cn": "投资就是要冒风险。"
}
],
