"phonetic_ldoce": "dɪˈstrɔɪ",
"pos": "v.",
"meaning": "破坏，毁灭；杀死，人道毁灭（受伤、生病或危险的动物）；彻底打败，击溃；毁掉……的生活，使垮掉",
"translations": [
"v. 破坏，毁灭；杀死，人道毁灭（受伤、生病或危险的动物）；彻底打败，击溃；毁掉……的生活，使垮掉"
],
"en_defs": [],
"examples": [
{
"en": "That's a sure recipe for destroying the economy and creating chaos.",
"cn": "那是一个摧毁经济、制造混乱的注定因素。"
},
{
"en": "If I was younger or more naive, the criticism would have destroyed me.",
"cn": "要是我年轻点儿或幼稚点儿，这批评可能已经把我毁了。"
},
{
"en": "Lindsay was unhurt but the horse had to be destroyed.",
"cn": "林赛没被伤着，但那匹马不得不被宰掉。"
},
{
"en": "The company produces chemicals that <b>destroy</b> ticks and mites.",
"cn": "该公司生产消灭壁虱和螨虫的化学品。"
},
{
"en": "The dispute could <b>destroy</b> Australia's hard-won reputation for industrial stability.",
"cn": "这场纠纷可能会摧毁澳大利亚辛苦得来的产业稳定声誉。"
},
{
"en": "The virus can actually <b>destroy</b> those white blood cells, leaving the body wide open to attack from other infections.",
"cn": "该病毒实际上能破坏那些白血球，使身体极易受到其他感染。"
}
],
