"pos": "n.",
"meaning": "偏见，成见，歧视；<法律>损害，侵害；使有偏见，使有成见； 损害，不利于",
"translations": [
"n. 偏见，成见，歧视；<法律>损害，侵害",
"v. 使有偏见，使有成见； 损害，不利于"
],
"en_defs": [],
"examples": [
{
"en": "There was a deep-rooted racial prejudice long before the two countries went to war.",
"cn": "早在两国交战之前就有了根深蒂固的种族偏见。"
},
{
"en": "There is widespread prejudice against workers over 45.",
"cn": "对年龄超过45岁的工人有普遍的偏见。"
},
{
"en": "I think your upbringing has prejudiced you.",
"cn": "我认为你的教养使你抱有偏见。"
},
{
"en": "The report was held back for fear of prejudicing his trial.",
"cn": "因为担心会使他的审判带有偏见，该报告没有公开。"
},
{
"en": "Her study was not in any way intended to prejudice the future development of the college.",
"cn": "她的研究绝对无意损害该学院的未来发展。"
},
{
"en": "I try to rise above <b>prejudice</b>.",
"cn": "我尽力摆脱偏见。"
}
],
