"phonetic_uk": "/ˌembriˈɒnɪk/",
"phonetic_ldoce": "ˌembriˈɒnɪk◂",
"pos": "adj.",
"meaning": "胚胎的，与胚胎有关的；萌芽阶段的，初期的；似胚胎的",
"translations": [
"adj. 胚胎的，与胚胎有关的；萌芽阶段的，初期的；似胚胎的"
],
"en_defs": [],
"examples": [
{
"en": "...Romania's embryonic democracy.",
"cn": "…罗马尼亚非常初期民主。"
},
{
"en": "At the time, he was trying to recruit members for his embryonic resistance group.",
"cn": "那时候他正在为他那萌芽中的抵抗组织招兵买马。"
},
{
"en": "Different from the <b>embryonic</b> stem cell we talked about before, it's an example of an adult stem cell.",
"cn": "和我们之前谈到的胚胎干细胞有所不同，这是一个成人干细胞的例子。"
},
{
"en": "Why people are so excited about <b>embryonic</b> stem cells is because in nature they become all the cells of the body.",
"cn": "胚胎干细胞如此让人激动是因为它的天然功能就是分化成身体所有的细胞。"
},
{
"en": "Other epigenetic processes appear to occur randomly, while others are normal, such as those that guide <b>embryonic</b> cells as they become heart, brain, or liver cells, for example.",
"cn": "其他的表观遗传过程似乎是随机发生的，而其他过程则是正常的，比如那些引导胚胎细胞成为心脏、大脑或肝细胞的过程。"
}
],
